# identuum-ui — Playwright credentials overlay for the
# IDP CE customer-smoke stack.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
# -----------------
# A gitignored, operator-controlled secrets file the Playwright runner
# auto-loads when `IDENTUUM_E2E_CE_CUSTOMER_SMOKE=1` is set (which the
# `pnpm e2e:ce-customer-smoke` script does). This file lives ALONGSIDE
# `.env.playwright.local` (the canonical dev-stack credentials file);
# the two stacks have separate first-run-wizard outputs so they
# typically need separate credentials.
#
# HOW TO USE
# ----------
# 1. Copy this template to its real name:
#       cp .env.playwright.customer-smoke.local.example .env.playwright.customer-smoke.local
# 2. Fill in the THREE site_admin lines below with the credentials YOU
#    chose at the M1 setup wizard against the customer-smoke stack
#    (host http://127.0.0.1:7124/setup). The customer-smoke wizard mints
#    its own site_admin row — it is independent of the dev-stack row.
# 3. Run the stable command from `identuum-ui`:
#       pnpm e2e:ce-customer-smoke
#
# HARD RULES (read before editing)
# --------------------------------
# - This file is gitignored via .env*.local in identuum-ui/.gitignore.
#   Verify with: git check-ignore .env.playwright.customer-smoke.local
# - NEVER commit the populated file. NEVER paste its contents into a
#   log, chat, screenshot, PR body, or report.
# - The values below are placeholders. Replace EACH placeholder with
#   real values. Do not leave a `REPLACE_ME` value in place — the
#   spec's pre-flight will refuse to silently run with placeholders.
# - The Playwright runner NEVER prints credential values. The runbook
#   at identuum-idp-ce/docs/CE_CUSTOMER_SMOKE_RUNBOOK.md enforces the
#   same discipline.

# Canonical site_admin email — match exactly what you entered at the
# M1 wizard. Default in most installs is `site_admin@system.local`.
IDENTUUM_TEST_SITE_ADMIN_EMAIL=REPLACE_ME_site_admin_email

# Plaintext site_admin password — what you typed at the M1 wizard.
# Treat this value like a production secret.
IDENTUUM_TEST_SITE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=REPLACE_ME_site_admin_password

# Base32-encoded TOTP secret for the site_admin's MFA enrollment. If
# the customer-smoke site_admin has NO MFA enrolled, leave the value
# unset (delete the line) and the spec will fail with a clear safe
# diagnostic naming MFA-not-enrolled as one of the three most likely
# causes. To complete a full PASS the site_admin row MUST have MFA
# enrolled; the customer-smoke wizard does NOT auto-enroll MFA so the
# operator must enroll via the bundled UI's /account/settings page
# before running this spec.
IDENTUUM_TEST_SITE_ADMIN_TOTP_SECRET=REPLACE_ME_site_admin_totp_secret_base32
